\name{runtime}
\alias{config_yytree}
\alias{quit_yytree}
\title{
Configure and stop the yytree Java runtime
}
\description{
\strong{\code{config_yytree()}:} Start or reuse the Java subprocess used by all yytree previews.

\strong{\code{quit_yytree()}:} Close all yytree windows, stop Java, and clear the saved runtime configuration.
}
\usage{
config_yytree(path2egps, max_memory_heap = "4g", max_memory_stack = "8m",
    restart = FALSE)
quit_yytree()
}
\arguments{
\item{path2egps}{\strong{\code{config_yytree} only:} Required. One existing eGPS installation-directory string containing \file{dependency-egps} JARs. The installation's \file{jre} is preferred; if absent, \env{JAVA_HOME} is used. Java 25 or newer is required. The package supplies its bridge JAR, not the eGPS core.}
\item{max_memory_heap}{\strong{\code{config_yytree} only:} One Java heap-limit string, default \code{"4g"}, passed as \code{-Xmx}. Positive integer followed by \code{m} or \code{g}, case-insensitive; for example \code{"512m"}. Changing a configured value requires \code{restart = TRUE}.}
\item{max_memory_stack}{\strong{\code{config_yytree} only:} One per-thread Java stack-size string, default \code{"8m"}, passed as \code{-Xss}. Positive integer followed by \code{k}, \code{m}, or \code{g}, case-insensitive; for example \code{"512k"} or \code{"16m"}. Changing a configured value requires \code{restart = TRUE}.}
\item{restart}{\strong{\code{config_yytree} only:} One nonmissing logical value, default \code{FALSE}. With \code{FALSE}, identical configuration reuses a live subprocess and changed configuration raises an error. \code{TRUE} closes all existing windows and restarts Java with the supplied configuration, even if unchanged.}
}
\details{
\subsection{config_yytree}{
Call this function before printing a plot. Loading the package and constructing plot values do not start Java. The first call starts one independent subprocess; all previews in this R session share it. No embedded rJava JVM or eGPS desktop main frame is used, and R's \env{JAVA_HOME} is not modified.

Heap and stack are separate resources: increasing heap does not fix stack overflow in a deeply nested tree. Both memory arguments are checked before launch. Startup failures report Java diagnostics; the returned log path helps diagnose later failures.

After an unexpected Java exit, the next print attempts to start a fresh subprocess from the last successful configuration and warns that old window state was lost. Communication failures, timeouts and user interrupts terminate the subprocess without replaying the in-flight request. Normal startup and requests have a 30-second timeout. Explicit quit clears the configuration and disables automatic recovery until configured again. R exit or package unload attempts to shut down Java. Logs are written below \file{tempdir()/yytree/logs}; the returned configuration gives the actual log path.
}
\subsection{quit_yytree}{
This function has no parameters. Calling it when Java is not running is safe, including repeated calls. A message reports whether Java was shut down or was already stopped. Plot specifications already stored in R remain unchanged. After quitting, call \code{config_yytree()} again before printing; explicit quit does not trigger automatic recovery.

Closing a preview window only disposes that window and keeps Java available. \code{quit_yytree()} instead terminates the subprocess and all of its windows.
}
}
\section{Similarities and differences}{
config_yytree starts or reuses one shared Java subprocess; quit_yytree stops it and clears configuration. Closing a window only closes that preview. To change heap, stack or installation settings, call config_yytree with restart = TRUE; to resume after quit_yytree, configure again explicitly.
}
\value{
\describe{
\item{\code{config_yytree()}}{Invisibly returns the effective configuration list: normalized installation root, Java directory, heap/stack settings, runtime probe information, process ID (\code{pid}) and stderr log path (\code{log}).}
\item{\code{quit_yytree()}}{Invisibly returns \code{NULL}.}
}
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{print.yytree}}, \code{\link{yytree}}
}
\examples{
# config_yytree()
\dontrun{
# Set EGPS_HOME to an existing eGPS installation directory first.
egps_home <- Sys.getenv("EGPS_HOME")
stopifnot(nzchar(egps_home), dir.exists(egps_home))
runtime <- config_yytree(egps_home)
p <- yytree("(A:1,B:2);") + leaf_labels()
print(p)
# Changing memory settings closes all existing previews.
runtime <- config_yytree(egps_home, max_memory_heap = "8g",
                         max_memory_stack = "16m", restart = TRUE)
quit_yytree()
}

# quit_yytree()
\dontrun{
egps_home <- Sys.getenv("EGPS_HOME")
stopifnot(nzchar(egps_home), dir.exists(egps_home))
config_yytree(egps_home)
p <- yytree("(A:1,B:2);")
print(p)
quit_yytree()
quit_yytree()  # Safe even after the subprocess has stopped.
config_yytree(egps_home)  # Required before printing again.
print(p)
quit_yytree()
}

}
